  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    # Collect non-zero colors\n    colors = sorted({v for row in grid for v in row if v != 0})\n    if not colors:\n        return grid\n\n    # Find largest connected component among all non-zero colors\n    visited = [[False] * w for _ in range(h)]\n    best_cells = None\n    best_color = None\n\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            color = grid[r][c]\n            if color == 0 or visited[r][c]:\n                continue\n\n            stack = [(r, c)]\n            visited[r][c] = True\n            cells = []\n\n            while stack:\n                x, y = stack.pop()\n                cells.append((x, y))\n                for dx, dy in ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)):\n                    nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n                    if 0 <= nx < h and 0 <= ny < w and not visited[nx][ny] and grid[nx][ny] == color:\n                        visited[nx][ny] = True\n                        stack.append((nx, ny))\n\n            if best_cells is None or len(cells) > len(best_cells):\n                best_cells = cells\n                best_color = color\n\n    # Assume there are exactly two roles: structure color and marker color.\n    # Marker color is the other non-zero color if present; otherwise use structure color.\n    other_colors = [c for c in colors if c != best_color]\n    marker_color = other_colors[0] if other_colors else best_color\n\n    # Bounding box of the selected structure\n    min_r = min(r for r, c in best_cells)\n    max_r = max(r for r, c in best_cells)\n    min_c = min(c for r, c in best_cells)\n    max_c = max(c for r, c in best_cells)\n\n    comp_set = set(best_cells)\n    out = []\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n            if (r, c) in comp_set or grid[r][c] == marker_color:\n                row.append(marker_color)\n            else:\n                row.append(0)\n        out.append(row)\n\n    return out",
